# Arguments for llama-server, consumed by llama-server.service.
# Single logical line, word-split by systemd. Restart after editing:
#   systemctl --user restart llama-server.service
#
# Bound to 127.0.0.1 on purpose: llama-server has no authentication.
# Model weights are cached under ~/.cache/llama.cpp (LLAMA_CACHE in the unit).
#
# The server runs in router mode: it serves every model in LLAMA_CACHE, picking
# one per request from the "model" field, and holds nothing at startup. Per-model
# flags (context, sampling) live in llama-models.ini; --models-preset is passed
# from the unit because %h does not expand in an EnvironmentFile.
#
# --models-max 1 is the point of the exercise on a 93 GB machine: loading a
# second model evicts the first rather than trying to hold both. Requesting a
# model that is not resident costs a full load (tens of seconds for a 50 GB
# model), so this trades switch latency for not parking 49.6 GB permanently.
#
# --sleep-idle-seconds is what actually reclaims memory: an idle child releases
# its weights and reports "sleeping" (measured here: 31 GB -> 11 GB), and the
# next request wakes it in ~8 s. --models-max only bounds concurrent residency.
LLAMA_SERVER_ARGS=--host 127.0.0.1 --port 8080 --models-max 1 --sleep-idle-seconds 900 --metrics
